WO-23 (rule-based detectors) + WO-25 (offline scoring) -- SURFACE live result.

Architecture (docs/ARCHITECTURE.md isolation rule honored):
  detection/detectors.py  -- pure per-domain detectors (state machines over live
                             feed events). NEVER read attack_logs.
  detection/run_detectors.py -- taps the LIVE feeds (MAVLink on tcp:5763:
                             GLOBAL_POSITION_INT / LOCAL_POSITION_NED / HEARTBEAT /
                             RC_CHANNELS; AIS UDP:10110) and appends Alerts to a
                             JSONL log. Runs blind.
  tools/score_detectors.py -- the ONLY reader of attack_logs/*.csv; replays the
                             blind alert log against ground-truth windows and
                             reports precision/recall per attack family.

Detectors:
  GpsJumpDetector          -- believed-position speed > plausible hull speed.
  AisConflictDetector      -- (a) own-MMSI AIS position vs the vessel's own
                              telemetry (impersonation), (b) invalid/fabricated
                              MMSI (ghost), (c) same-MMSI teleport. The own-vessel
                              MMSI is whitelisted (operational knowledge, not
                              ground truth) so the real vessel is never mis-flagged.
  C2OverrideDetector       -- any RC override / driven RC channel = actuator seizure.
  AcousticDivergenceDetector (underwater) -- believed position drifting while the
                              AUV is UNPROPELLED (disarmed) = external-nav/acoustic
                              spoof; catches the stealthy slow ramp a speed gate misses.

LIVE SURFACE RUN (detector blind; attacks fired live; then scored vs ground truth):
  attack             TP   FP  windows  detected   prec  recall
  ais_spoof          11    0        1         1   1.00    1.00
  c2_replay           2    0        1         1   1.00    1.00
  gps_spoof           2    0        1         1   1.00    1.00
  OVERALL            15    0        3         3   1.00    1.00

  - No false positive on the legitimate vessel (own MMSI 123456789 at its true
    position was correctly NOT flagged; the impersonator's 123456789 reports
    ~755 m off the vessel's own telemetry WERE flagged).
  Alert log: evidence/detector_alerts_wamv_run.jsonl.

Underwater detectors (acoustic-divergence + C2) validated in detection self-test
(detection/detectors.py logic); live underwater run recorded separately.

LIVE UNDERWATER RUN (detector blind; acoustic_spoof + c2 fired; scored):
  attack             TP   FP  windows  detected   prec  recall
  acoustic_spoof     15    4        1         1   0.79    1.00
  c2_replay           3    0        1         1   1.00    1.00
  OVERALL            18    4        2         2   0.82    1.00

  - acoustic_spoof recall 1.00 (every spoof caught: the AUV's believed position
    drifting while UNPROPELLED). Precision 0.79 -- the simple drift-while-disarmed
    rule also fires on the brief settling transient just after an armed override,
    an honest limitation; an INS-vs-acoustic residual detector would tighten it.
  - The scoring harness quantifying imperfect precision is exactly its purpose.
  Alert log: evidence/detector_alerts_bluerov2_run.jsonl.

BOTH DOMAINS: recall 1.00 (every attack in every applicable family detected);
surface precision 1.00, underwater precision 0.82.
